  "id": "lookups",
  "sectionId": "golden-lookups",
  "title": "Fast lookups: hash tables and search trees",
  "tier": "intermediate",
  "minutes": 20,
  "objectives": [
    "Explain how a hash table finds a key in about one step",
    "Show what a collision is and what resizing does",
    "Choose between a hash table and a balanced search tree"
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "title": "A million usernames",
      "intent": "hook",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "hook-text",
          "kind": "prose",
          "markdown": "Checking whether a username is taken by scanning a list of a million names takes up to a million comparisons. A **hash table** jumps straight to the right place; a **balanced search tree** gets there in about 20 steps.\n\nBoth are everywhere: `Map`, `dict` and `HashMap` are hash tables; database indexes are trees."
        },
        {
          "id": "anagram-guess",
          "kind": "predict",
          "question": "With 5 buckets and a hash that adds up the character codes, do \"cat\" and \"act\" land in the same bucket?",
          "options": ["Yes", "No"],
          "answer": 0,
          "expected": null,
          "reveal": { "block": "hash-demo", "step": "insert-act" },
          "explanation": "Both have the same letters, so the same sum: 312. 312 mod 5 is 2 for both. That's a collision."
        }
      ]
    },
