          "id": "range-query",
          "kind": "quiz",
          "question": "You need every username between \"ada\" and \"bob\", in order. Which structure fits?",
          "code": null,
          "options": [
            "A hash table",
            "A balanced search tree",
            "Either, equally",
            "Neither"
          ],
          "correct": [1],
          "explanation": "A search tree keeps keys sorted, so it can walk from \"ada\" to \"bob\" in order. A hash table scatters keys and would have to check them all."
        }
